WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.920
Meet two countries, A and B.

2
00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:07.170
With all its resources, A
can make 600 tonnes of food.

3
00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.720
B can make only 240.

4
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:13.730
For cloth, it's 300 rolls against 240.

5
00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.330
A is ahead again.

6
00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:18.420
So should A make everything itself?

7
00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.770
Real countries face this choice too.

8
00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:22.910
Why do they buy from
abroad things they could

9
00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:24.940
make perfectly well at home?

10
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.940
In this mission, you'll
pull apart two ideas:

11
00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.160
absolute advantage and
comparative advantage.

12
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.090
Then you'll test terms of
trade in the graph lab,

13
00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.880
to see when both countries gain,

14
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.780
and who gains more.

15
00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:42.190
Your mission: explain why trading
can beat doing it all yourself.
